    {
      "text": "8.3.2. COMPARISON BETWEEN NEURAL KOOPMAN LIFTINGS AND POLYNOMIAL LIFTINGS",
      "bbox": [
        90.27301025390625,
        303.5846252441406,
        507.5125427246094,
        313.33734130859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We compare root mean square error (RMSE) between a polynomial-lifted extended dynamic mode",
      "bbox": [
        90.00000762939453,
        322.89361572265625,
        522.0001831054688,
        332.6463317871094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "decomposition baseline and our neural lifting approach on the Hopper system. For the polyno-",
      "bbox": [
        90.00000762939453,
        336.443603515625,
        522.0001831054688,
        346.1963195800781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "mial lift, we use PyKoopman (Pan et al., 2024) with degree-3 monomials and identical training",
      "bbox": [
        90.00000762939453,
        349.99261474609375,
        522.0000610351562,
        359.7453308105469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "data/preprocessing. During open-loop evaluation, the polynomial model becomes numerically un-",
      "bbox": [
        90.00000762939453,
        363.5416259765625,
        522.0001220703125,
        373.2943420410156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "stable, that is, its predictions grow without bound and diverge by the eighth timestep, so we report",
      "bbox": [
        90.00000762939453,
        377.09063720703125,
        522.0004272460938,
        386.8433532714844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "RMSE only over the first 5 prediction steps in Table 2. In contrast, our neural lifting yields a stable",
      "bbox": [
        90.00000762939453,
        390.6396484375,
        522.0000610351562,
        400.3923645019531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "latent dynamics model that tracks accurately across three complete hops, enabling longer-horizon",
      "bbox": [
        90.00000762939453,
        404.18865966796875,
        522.0001831054688,
        413.9413757324219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "evaluation. These results highlight that for certain systems, e.g., those with strongly nonlinear,",
      "bbox": [
        90.00000762939453,
        417.7386474609375,
        522.0003051757812,
        427.4913635253906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "contact-rich dynamics (like the MuJoCo hopper), fixed polynomial bases are insufficient, whereas",
      "bbox": [
        90.00000762939453,
        431.28765869140625,
        522.0003051757812,
        441.0403747558594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "a neural network lifting function captures the necessary structure and remains stable over extended",
      "bbox": [
        90.00000762939453,
        444.836669921875,
        522.000244140625,
        454.5893859863281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "rollouts. Together, these results motivate the development of a Koopman reachable-set computation",
      "bbox": [
        90.00000762939453,
        458.38568115234375,
        522.0001220703125,
        468.1383972167969
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "framework that incorporates neural networks in the loop, which we enable using auto LiRPA.",
      "bbox": [
        90.00000762939453,
        471.9346923828125,
        508.63262939453125,
        481.6883544921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
